=head2 SDL_GetPlatform

  my $result = SDL_GetPlatform();

C: C<< const char * SDL_GetPlatform(void) >>

Get the name of the platform.

Here are the names returned for some (but not all) supported platforms:

- "Windows" - "macOS" - "Linux" - "iOS" - "Android"

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

Returns string: the name of the platform. If the correct platform name is not available, returns a string beginning with the text "Unknown".

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.



